From b4d8abf031e0ae33a43ad812c7dc768b973199dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 12:22:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat: port h2p working pipeline (IR v1.2.0, extractor,
 mapper, 4-layer validation)

Byte-faithful port of the verified h2p implementation with two path
adaptations: src/map/ -> src/mapper/ (repo convention) and the OOXML
normalizer import now targets the dom-to-pptx subtree at
third_party/subtrees/dom-to-pptx (per third_party/subtrees.toml,
decision adopt_subtree; the h2p-verified vendor file is byte-identical
to upstream master).

- src/ir: IR contract v1.2.0 (invariants I1-I9) + runtime validator
- src/extract: WeasyPrint box tree -> IR (tables, opacity, clipping,
  images, 2-tier SVG chart recovery)
- src/mapper: IR -> editable PPTX via PptxGenJS + subtree normalizer
- src/validate: Layer A/B (text+media), Layer C (masked pixel diff),
  Layer D (IR-vs-OOXML IoU)
- run.sh orchestrator (parallel validation subflows), setup_mac.sh,
  package.json/-lock (pptxgenjs, pixelmatch, pngjs, jszip, xmldom)
- .gitignore: node_modules/, out/, third_party/repos/

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
