+# src/extract — HTML → Visual Object IR
+
+`weasy_extract.py` renders HTML with WeasyPrint (deterministic, rule-based CSS
+layout engine — no browser required) and walks the box tree into IR v1.2.0
+(`src/ir/schema.ts`). Handles multi-page decks, tables (grid_x/colspan/rowspan),
+opacity products, overflow:hidden clipping, images (document-order src queue),
+and two-tier SVG chart recovery (data-* attrs first, mark/axis reverse-engineering
+second; unparseable → fallbackRegion).
+
+The architecture docs describe a Playwright-based extractor; WeasyPrint is the
+v0.1 implementation choice (see docs/lessons.md #3). Read docs/lessons.md and
+docs/HANDOFF.md §5 footguns before editing.
+
+```
+python3 src/extract/weasy_extract.py fixtures/deck.html out/deck.ir.json
+```
